{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law cap and return deadline","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit above one and one-half times one month's rent, may not raise it more than 10% a year, and must return the deposit with interest within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; 10% annual increase","coverage_conditions":"All residential rentals in New Jersey; security-deposit account and interest rules do not apply to seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Security deposits for seasonal use or rental (a term of not more than 125 consecutive days for a person with a permanent residence elsewhere) are exempt from the deposit account provisions.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount of the security deposit wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic-violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and notify the tenant within three business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease because they or their child face an imminent threat of serious physical harm from a named person; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
